-- title:
--   Theorem 6 (Subsequence Convergence)
-- statement:
--   Suppose that Assumptions 1, 2 and 4 hold and that the parameters are chosen as in (64) and (65). Let $\{(w^k;u^k;z^k;v^k)\}_{k\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence generated by IALM satisfying the stopping criteria (32), and let $(w^*;u^*;z^*;v^*)$ be an accumulation point of it. Then $v^*=w^*$ and $(w^*;u^*;z^*)$ is a P-stationary triplet of (2), with the constant $\alpha=1/\rho$:
--   $$
--   \nabla f(w^*)+A^\top z^*=0,\qquad u^*\in\mathrm{Prox}_{\alpha\lambda\|(\cdot)_+\|_0}(u^*+\alpha z^*),\qquad Aw^*+b=u^* .
--   $$
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: a sequence generated by IALM, whose primal step is computed by 0/1-BALM (Algorithm 2) → every sequence satisfying (32a), (32b), (33) and vᵏ⁺¹ = wᵏ⁺¹ with positive tolerances; reason: every 0/1-BALM sequence satisfies these relations, and the proof in the paper uses only these relations
--   - generalization: Assumption 2 with γ := √θ_min(AAᵀ) > 0 → any γ > 0 with γ‖z‖ ≤ ‖Aᵀz‖ for every z; reason: the paper’s γ satisfies this inequality, so the printed statement is the instance γ = √θ_min(AAᵀ), and the proof uses Assumption 2 only through this inequality
--   - generalization: (w*; u*; z*) is a P-stationary triplet, that is, (27) holds for some α > 0 → (27) holds with α = 1/ρ; reason: the proof gives (80) with the constant α = 1/ρ of the algorithm, and this implies the existential form of Definition 2
--   - encoding: A ∈ ℝⁿˣᵖ and its transpose Aᵀ → a continuous linear map between Euclidean spaces and its adjoint; reason: the same objects in the standard bases
--   - encoding: accumulation point → MapClusterPt along atTop; reason: in a first-countable space this is the limit of a subsequence
-- source:
--   Zhang & Xiu, Global Convergence of Inexact Augmented Lagrangian Method for Zero-One Composite Optimization, arXiv:2112.00440v1, Theorem 6, p.25

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Assumptions
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Parameters
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Run
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_PStationary

open Filter Topology

namespace ZeroOneIALM

/-- Theorem 6 (Subsequence Convergence), Zhang & Xiu, arXiv:2112.00440v1, p.25: under Assumptions
1, 2 and 4 and the parameter choices (64), (65), if `(w*; u*; z*; v*)` is an accumulation point of
an IALM sequence satisfying (32), then `v* = w*` and `(w*; u*; z*)` is a P-stationary triplet of
(2), with the constant `α = 1/ρ` of the algorithm.

**Formalization Note.** An accumulation point is a cluster point of the sequence
(`MapClusterPt`). Definition 2 asks for some `α > 0`; the proof gives (80) with `α = 1/ρ`, and
this is what the conclusion records. -/
theorem theorem_6 {p n : ℕ} {f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) → ℝ}
    {A : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    {b : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} {lam μ ρ lf γ η : ℝ} {ε : ℕ → ℝ}
    {w : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)} {u z : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    {v : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)}
    (hlam : 0 < lam) (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (h1 : IsSmoothWith f lf) (h2 : IsRowRankConstant A γ) (h4 : IsCoercive f)
    (hpar : IsParameterChoice μ lf γ ρ η ε)
    (hrun : IsIALMRun f A b lam μ ρ ε w u z v)
    {wstar vstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)} {ustar zstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    (hcluster : MapClusterPt (wstar, ustar, zstar, vstar) atTop
      (fun k => (w k, u k, z k, v k))) :
    vstar = wstar ∧ IsPStationaryWith f A b lam (1 / ρ) wstar ustar zstar := by sorry

end ZeroOneIALM
